  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical charged particles each having a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> are placed on a horizontal table with a separation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> between them such that they stay in limited equilibrium. If the coefficient of friction between each particle and the table is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>, find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. [Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ]",
    "image": null
  },
